1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:02,335
[BEA] <i>You know what, Abi?</i>

2
00:00:02,419 --> 00:00:05,171
<i>He went to see Billy first…</i>

3
00:00:05,255 --> 00:00:06,256
[SNIFFLING]

4
00:00:06,339 --> 00:00:08,508
<i>…before even coming to his own family.</i>

5
00:00:09,259 --> 00:00:11,469
<i>What are we to him?</i>

6
00:00:14,264 --> 00:00:15,765
<i>Trash?</i>

7
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:19,686
<i>Just trash.</i>

8
00:00:20,228 --> 00:00:23,440
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

9
00:00:23,523 --> 00:00:24,774
[GRUNTS]

10
00:00:24,858 --> 00:00:27,235
<i>Where do you think you're going?</i>

11
00:00:27,318 --> 00:00:28,737
<i>Damn you!</i>

12
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:32,532
[GRUNTING, GROANING]

13
00:00:32,615 --> 00:00:34,117
[BEA] <i>Get off me!</i>

14
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:35,535
<i>You witch!</i>

15
00:00:35,618 --> 00:00:40,665
[GRUNTING, GROANING]

16
00:00:40,749 --> 00:00:41,875
- [KICK LANDS]
- [GROANS]

17
00:00:43,626 --> 00:00:47,297
<i>What do you want, huh?</i>
<i>Is this what you want?</i>

18
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:50,759
<i>- Damn you, you witch!</i> [SLAP LANDS]
- [BEA GROANING]

19
00:00:50,842 --> 00:00:54,137
<i>What more do you want from me, huh?!</i>

20
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:57,307
<i>Leave us alone! Damn you!</i>

21
00:00:57,974 --> 00:00:59,893
<i>They just let Bea go?!</i>

22
00:00:59,976 --> 00:01:02,937
[BILLY]<i> I'm tired of getting my hopes</i>
<i>up for nothing, Auntie.</i>

23
00:01:04,230 --> 00:01:07,400
<i>So I'll put a stop to them myself.</i>

24
00:01:12,781 --> 00:01:15,075
<i>Hello, Jordan? Where are you?</i>

25
00:01:15,867 --> 00:01:17,077
[JORDAN] <i>Summit Bay Suites.</i>

26
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:18,745
<i>We've been here before.</i>

27
00:01:18,828 --> 00:01:20,830
<i>This is where Peter was staying.</i>

28
00:01:21,623 --> 00:01:23,458
<i>This can't be a coincidence.</i>

29
00:01:23,541 --> 00:01:24,834
[BILLY] <i>Why?</i>

30
00:01:24,918 --> 00:01:26,878
[JORDAN] <i>This is where</i>
<i>I traced the location</i>

31
00:01:26,961 --> 00:01:29,130
<i>of the person who leaked LoveList's files.</i>

32
00:01:29,631 --> 00:01:31,049
[BILLY] <i>Okay. I'm going there.</i>

33
00:01:31,132 --> 00:01:32,050
[JORDAN] <i>Okay.</i>

34
00:01:32,133 --> 00:01:37,514
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

35
00:01:42,018 --> 00:01:43,937
<i>Dude. Where is she?</i>

36
00:01:44,687 --> 00:01:46,523
<i>- I lost her.</i>
<i>- Huh?!</i>

37
00:01:48,066 --> 00:01:49,526
<i>She suddenly disappeared!</i>

38
00:01:49,609 --> 00:01:52,529
<i>I'm sorry. I asked reception,</i>
<i>but they don't want to tell me anything.</i>

39
00:01:52,612 --> 00:01:54,906
<i>How did you lose her, Jordan?</i>

40
00:01:55,949 --> 00:01:57,117
<i>Sorry.</i>

41
00:01:58,952 --> 00:02:00,703
<i>Wait. Dude.</i>

42
00:02:01,371 --> 00:02:02,664
<i>Is that Peter?</i>

43
00:02:04,207 --> 00:02:05,542
<i>Remember the leaked files?</i>

44
00:02:05,625 --> 00:02:07,752
<i>It was uploaded from this hotel.</i>

45
00:02:08,670 --> 00:02:10,922
[BILLY] <i>You were talking to Bea.</i>

46
00:02:11,005 --> 00:02:13,174
<i>Bea Mercado, right?</i>

47
00:02:13,758 --> 00:02:14,759
[EXHALES SHARPLY]

48
00:02:18,638 --> 00:02:20,431
<i>I'll tell you everything.</i>

49
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:25,895
[BEA] <i>Sir, wait a minute!</i>
<i>Wait a minute!</i>

50
00:02:25,979 --> 00:02:27,856
<i>Mariela Mercado, we have</i>
<i>a warrant for your arrest.</i>

51
00:02:27,939 --> 00:02:28,982
<i>Go away!</i>

52
00:02:29,065 --> 00:02:32,443
<i>We are charging you</i>
<i>with qualified trespass to dwelling,</i>

53
00:02:32,527 --> 00:02:36,072
<i>frustrated murder, and reckless</i>
<i>imprudence resulting in arson.</i>

54
00:02:36,156 --> 00:02:37,866
<i>- Go ahead, cuff her!</i>
<i>- Sir, wait a minute!</i>

55
00:02:37,949 --> 00:02:38,992
<i>Wait! Arrest me instead!</i>

56
00:02:39,075 --> 00:02:41,619
<i>Spare my mother!</i>
<i>Take me instead! Please!</i>

57
00:02:41,703 --> 00:02:44,998
- <i>You're all animals!</i>
- <i>Ma, no!</i>

58
00:02:45,081 --> 00:02:46,166
<i>Cuff her!</i>

59
00:02:46,749 --> 00:02:49,669
<i>Billy, please! Not my mother!</i>
<i>Take me instead!</i>

60
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:52,505
<i>What? Are you scared?</i>

61
00:02:53,131 --> 00:02:54,173
<i>Don't worry.</i>

62
00:02:55,466 --> 00:02:57,886
<i>Your daughter will be with you in jail.</i>

63
00:02:59,053 --> 00:03:01,431
<i>We'll be the ones messing</i>
<i>with your life this time.</i>

64
00:03:01,514 --> 00:03:07,770
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

65
00:03:12,233 --> 00:03:13,276
[EXHALES SHARPLY]

66
00:03:14,235 --> 00:03:15,236
Dude.

67
00:03:15,945 --> 00:03:16,821
Finally!

68
00:03:17,530 --> 00:03:18,615
It's over!

69
00:03:22,577 --> 00:03:23,953
Damn you!

70
00:03:24,579 --> 00:03:26,539
[MARIELA] You are the ones
who should go to prison!

71
00:03:26,623 --> 00:03:28,249
You should pay!

72
00:03:29,334 --> 00:03:31,920
I'll get back at you,
especially you, Billy.

73
00:03:32,003 --> 00:03:34,797
I'll get back at you, you bastard!

74
00:03:35,423 --> 00:03:37,634
[OFFICER] That's enough. Take her in.

75
00:03:37,717 --> 00:03:44,432
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

76
00:04:00,573 --> 00:04:06,120
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

77
00:04:15,296 --> 00:04:22,011
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

78
00:05:00,758 --> 00:05:01,718
[CAR HORN HONKING]

79
00:05:01,801 --> 00:05:08,766
[SIREN BLARING]

80
00:05:08,850 --> 00:05:15,773
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

81
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:22,864
- [ENRICO] <i>You bought a lot, huh?</i>
<i>- Daddy!</i> [GIGGLES]

82
00:05:22,947 --> 00:05:24,866
- [OLIVE] <i>My goodness.</i>
<i>- Pa?</i>

83
00:05:24,949 --> 00:05:27,410
- [OLIVE] <i>She's such a daddy's girl!</i>
- [ENRICO] <i>Are you happy now?</i>

84
00:05:27,493 --> 00:05:29,537
- [YOUNG BILLY] <i>Yes. Thank you, Daddy.</i>
<i>- Pa?</i>

85
00:05:29,620 --> 00:05:33,333
- [WOMAN] <i>Oh! Watch where you're going.</i>
- [ENRICO] <i>Okay, let's go.</i>

86
00:05:33,416 --> 00:05:35,001
[OLIVE] <i>Come on, let's hurry up.</i>

87
00:05:36,419 --> 00:05:37,879
<i>Wear your seat belt, dear.</i>

88
00:05:37,962 --> 00:05:39,380
[YOUNG BILLY GIGGLING] <i>Yes.</i>

89
00:05:39,464 --> 00:05:41,549
- [OLIVE] <i>We're so happy.</i>
- [BEA] <i>Pa.</i>

90
00:05:41,632 --> 00:05:43,718
<i>Pa. Pa!</i>

91
00:05:43,801 --> 00:05:44,969
<i>Pa!</i>

92
00:05:46,429 --> 00:05:47,597
<i>Pa.</i>

93
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:49,182
<i>But the question is,</i>

94
00:05:50,224 --> 00:05:53,144
<i>which one of us is the bigger thief?</i>

95
00:05:54,604 --> 00:05:55,938
<i>A thief?</i>

96
00:05:57,940 --> 00:05:59,692
<i>What the hell are you talking about?</i>

97
00:06:01,778 --> 00:06:03,446
<i>If only you knew.</i>

98
00:06:04,572 --> 00:06:05,865
<i>Knew what?</i>

99
00:06:08,659 --> 00:06:10,953
<i>Why don't you just tell the truth,</i>

100
00:06:11,037 --> 00:06:13,706
<i>so I can understand</i>
<i>where your anger is coming from?</i>

101
00:06:17,126 --> 00:06:19,587
<i>What's your reason for going after me?</i>

102
00:06:22,131 --> 00:06:24,258
<i>Ma. Ma!</i>

103
00:06:26,803 --> 00:06:28,096
<i>Let go of my mother.</i>

104
00:06:28,179 --> 00:06:32,934
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

105
00:06:35,144 --> 00:06:36,771
<i>Leave my daughter alone!</i>

106
00:06:36,854 --> 00:06:38,523
<i>- Ma.</i>
<i>- Karma will get you one day!</i>

107
00:06:38,606 --> 00:06:39,774
<i>I'll be waiting.</i>

108
00:06:45,279 --> 00:06:48,241
<i>I can't bear to see you suffer, my dear.</i>

109
00:06:48,324 --> 00:06:50,326
<i>Me? Suffering?</i>

110
00:06:50,409 --> 00:06:51,619
<i>I'm not suffering.</i>

111
00:06:51,702 --> 00:06:53,454
<i>I never said I was suffering.</i>

112
00:06:53,538 --> 00:06:54,747
<i>I'll find a way.</i>

113
00:06:54,831 --> 00:06:56,749
<i>I'll get a job and then…</i>

114
00:06:56,833 --> 00:06:58,960
<i>I'll get back at Billy.</i>

115
00:06:59,043 --> 00:07:02,421
<i>I promise you. I'll make her pay.</i>

116
00:07:02,505 --> 00:07:07,969
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

117
00:07:12,807 --> 00:07:14,517
<i>Caloy, I don't understand.</i>

118
00:07:15,268 --> 00:07:19,105
<i>I've done everything I can</i>

119
00:07:19,772 --> 00:07:22,442
<i>to give my mother a good life.</i>

120
00:07:23,734 --> 00:07:24,902
[BEA SNIFFLES]

121
00:07:26,070 --> 00:07:27,530
<i>What's happening?</i>

122
00:07:28,197 --> 00:07:30,324
<i>I'm back to square one.</i>

123
00:07:30,408 --> 00:07:34,162
<i>I want Billy's life</i>
<i>because it should've been mine.</i>

124
00:07:35,204 --> 00:07:38,749
<i>That should've been mine,</i>
<i>but Billy just had to steal it!</i>

125
00:07:38,833 --> 00:07:43,254
[POLICE SIREN WAILING]

126
00:07:45,798 --> 00:07:52,138
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES, FADES]

127
00:08:04,192 --> 00:08:08,821
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

128
00:08:27,924 --> 00:08:33,221
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

129
00:08:47,902 --> 00:08:51,239
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES, FADES]

130
00:08:51,322 --> 00:08:53,950
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

131
00:08:54,033 --> 00:09:00,831
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING]

132
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:13,928
[INMATE 1] Wow.

133
00:09:14,011 --> 00:09:15,721
[INMATES CHATTERING]

134
00:09:15,805 --> 00:09:17,723
- What good skin.
- She's pretty.

135
00:09:18,391 --> 00:09:25,273
[CUFFS CLINKING]

136
00:09:26,274 --> 00:09:29,151
[CELL LOCK RATTLING]

137
00:09:29,235 --> 00:09:30,444
[CELL DOOR OPENS]

138
00:09:30,528 --> 00:09:33,656
[CUFFS CLINKING]

139
00:09:39,036 --> 00:09:40,413
- [CELL DOOR CLOSES]
- Ma, sit down.

140
00:09:40,496 --> 00:09:43,583
[CELL LOCK RATTLING]

141
00:09:43,666 --> 00:09:48,921
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

142
00:10:18,868 --> 00:10:23,706
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

143
00:10:45,895 --> 00:10:51,817
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

144
00:11:02,953 --> 00:11:08,209
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES, FADES]

145
00:11:08,292 --> 00:11:10,252
[BILLY] Um, Auntie Pres,

146
00:11:10,336 --> 00:11:12,630
this will be your room.

147
00:11:12,713 --> 00:11:14,924
And this'll be mine.

148
00:11:15,758 --> 00:11:18,010
And Oliver will stay there.

149
00:11:18,094 --> 00:11:19,345
As well as Dad.

150
00:11:19,428 --> 00:11:21,889
- Mmm.
- [PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

151
00:11:21,972 --> 00:11:24,392
You're letting your father
live here with us?

152
00:11:25,893 --> 00:11:27,895
Are you sure about this, Billy?

153
00:11:30,314 --> 00:11:34,235
What he did to my brother and me
isn't easy to forget.

154
00:11:36,612 --> 00:11:41,200
But I also can't forget
what he did for us.

155
00:11:44,495 --> 00:11:45,538
Mmm.

156
00:11:45,621 --> 00:11:49,792
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

157
00:11:49,875 --> 00:11:56,215
[MUSIC BECOMES GENTLE]

158
00:11:56,298 --> 00:11:57,716
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

159
00:11:57,800 --> 00:12:02,346
[WHEELCHAIR RATTLING]

160
00:12:02,430 --> 00:12:03,681
Go easy.

161
00:12:06,142 --> 00:12:07,017
[BILLY] Here, Dad.

162
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:09,228
- [ENRICO] Okay.
- Okay.

163
00:12:09,311 --> 00:12:11,772
- [BILLY] One, two, three.
- [OLIVER] Two, one.

164
00:12:13,065 --> 00:12:14,400
[PRECIOUS] I'll take care of it.

165
00:12:14,483 --> 00:12:17,027
[WHEELCHAIR RATTLING]

166
00:12:17,111 --> 00:12:18,737
[BILLY] Everything okay, Dad?

167
00:12:18,821 --> 00:12:19,905
Okay.

168
00:12:26,871 --> 00:12:28,080
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

169
00:12:31,750 --> 00:12:33,043
Oh.

170
00:12:33,127 --> 00:12:34,420
[OLIVER] Auntie.

171
00:12:34,503 --> 00:12:36,297
Thank you. Pa.

172
00:12:36,380 --> 00:12:37,798
Careful. Oops.

173
00:12:37,882 --> 00:12:39,216
[ENRICO GROANING]

174
00:12:40,092 --> 00:12:40,926
[OLIVER] Pa.

175
00:12:41,010 --> 00:12:42,303
- Here, Pa.
- [GROANS]

176
00:12:42,386 --> 00:12:43,554
Oh.

177
00:12:44,555 --> 00:12:47,808
Pa, did you know that we're
sharing a room?

178
00:12:47,892 --> 00:12:50,311
- Really?
- Come on, let's go!

179
00:12:50,394 --> 00:12:52,563
[OLIVER] Pa, hurry!

180
00:12:52,646 --> 00:12:55,357
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

181
00:12:55,441 --> 00:12:57,776
[OLIVER] As long as you
let me secure my spot!

182
00:13:09,371 --> 00:13:10,956
Pa, look at this.

183
00:13:11,457 --> 00:13:13,167
I had this printed myself!

184
00:13:13,250 --> 00:13:14,710
Looks good, huh?

185
00:13:14,793 --> 00:13:17,505
Before, we used to just be
together in photos.

186
00:13:17,588 --> 00:13:19,632
Now, we really are together!

187
00:13:19,715 --> 00:13:26,388
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

188
00:13:28,098 --> 00:13:28,974
Pa?

189
00:13:29,058 --> 00:13:34,522
[ENRICO CRYING]

190
00:13:36,524 --> 00:13:37,525
Pa.

191
00:13:44,156 --> 00:13:44,990
Pa?

192
00:13:45,074 --> 00:13:50,412
[KEEPS CRYING]

193
00:13:52,248 --> 00:13:58,128
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

194
00:14:07,930 --> 00:14:08,973
Thank you.

195
00:14:20,025 --> 00:14:21,151
[SOFT THUD]

196
00:14:22,778 --> 00:14:23,946
[LIGHTLY KNOCKING]

197
00:14:24,905 --> 00:14:26,949
Ah, come in, Billy.

198
00:14:27,032 --> 00:14:27,950
Um…

199
00:14:29,535 --> 00:14:32,621
You left some of your other stuff
at the apartment.

200
00:14:32,705 --> 00:14:33,998
I'll go back and get it.

201
00:14:34,081 --> 00:14:35,541
No, let me.

202
00:14:39,628 --> 00:14:41,422
I found these.

203
00:14:45,718 --> 00:14:47,303
I've read all of them too.

204
00:14:47,386 --> 00:14:50,431
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

205
00:14:50,514 --> 00:14:52,182
Those were for every year

206
00:14:52,808 --> 00:14:54,685
that I couldn't be with you, Billy.

207
00:14:57,354 --> 00:14:59,940
Thank you for letting me stay here.

208
00:15:01,901 --> 00:15:04,278
I just want to express my gratitude.

209
00:15:04,945 --> 00:15:06,947
If it weren't for you, I probably…

210
00:15:08,073 --> 00:15:12,494
I probably wouldn't be
with Auntie Pres and Oliver.

211
00:15:14,538 --> 00:15:17,666
You shouldn't feel like
you owe me anything, Billy.

212
00:15:19,501 --> 00:15:21,253
I'm the one who made

213
00:15:21,337 --> 00:15:22,880
many mistakes.

214
00:15:23,923 --> 00:15:25,925
I'm the one who made
so many wrong decisions.

215
00:15:27,968 --> 00:15:29,094
Billy.

216
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:34,224
Would it be okay if I asked for a hug?

217
00:15:34,308 --> 00:15:41,273
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

218
00:16:04,588 --> 00:16:07,675
[MUSIC SWELLS]

219
00:16:07,758 --> 00:16:10,177
[SOBBING]

220
00:16:17,685 --> 00:16:19,353
[SNIFFLES]

221
00:16:33,283 --> 00:16:34,535
[MUSIC FADES]

222
00:16:34,618 --> 00:16:36,078
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

223
00:16:36,161 --> 00:16:37,246
Auntie Pres.

224
00:16:40,457 --> 00:16:42,209
Your father

225
00:16:42,292 --> 00:16:45,295
is asking about the fire.

226
00:16:45,379 --> 00:16:47,631
He wants to know what really happened.

227
00:16:48,549 --> 00:16:50,259
What did you say, Auntie?

228
00:16:50,342 --> 00:16:53,637
I told him what you told me.

229
00:16:53,721 --> 00:16:55,639
That it was an accident.

230
00:16:56,432 --> 00:16:59,059
The doctors specifically told us

231
00:16:59,143 --> 00:17:01,270
that he isn't allowed to be stressed.

232
00:17:01,854 --> 00:17:05,816
It might stress him out
if he finds out someone is bothering us.

233
00:17:05,899 --> 00:17:06,984
[PRECIOUS] Hmm.

234
00:17:07,067 --> 00:17:10,029
It's good that it's not on the news much.

235
00:17:10,112 --> 00:17:12,406
It's good that he doesn't know
what really happened.

236
00:17:12,489 --> 00:17:14,908
And besides, they're both in jail now.

237
00:17:14,992 --> 00:17:16,285
Thank God.

238
00:17:16,368 --> 00:17:18,495
I can finally sleep peacefully.

239
00:17:20,247 --> 00:17:21,915
Me too, Auntie.

240
00:17:21,999 --> 00:17:24,543
I'll focus on LoveList first.

241
00:17:26,086 --> 00:17:27,921
I have a lot I need to recover.

242
00:17:28,005 --> 00:17:35,012
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING, FADES]

243
00:17:35,679 --> 00:17:36,764
Ma.

244
00:17:39,767 --> 00:17:41,518
No matter what happens,

245
00:17:43,103 --> 00:17:44,646
don't tell them

246
00:17:44,730 --> 00:17:47,608
that you know
they're Papa's second family.

247
00:17:48,942 --> 00:17:50,152
Why not?

248
00:17:50,778 --> 00:17:51,987
That's the truth.

249
00:17:52,571 --> 00:17:53,781
Ma.

250
00:17:54,656 --> 00:17:56,366
Please listen to me.

251
00:17:58,786 --> 00:18:00,829
That's a strong motive.

252
00:18:00,913 --> 00:18:04,875
It'll just prove that you're going after
Papa's illegitimate child.

253
00:18:04,958 --> 00:18:07,169
We'll get into more trouble.

254
00:18:07,252 --> 00:18:10,005
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

255
00:18:10,089 --> 00:18:11,131
But

256
00:18:11,924 --> 00:18:14,593
shouldn't they be the ones to suffer?

257
00:18:14,676 --> 00:18:15,636
Right?

258
00:18:16,512 --> 00:18:17,971
Not us.

259
00:18:18,847 --> 00:18:20,849
Especially not you.

260
00:18:23,227 --> 00:18:24,436
I'm sorry.

261
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:26,980
I'm sorry I dragged you into this.

262
00:18:27,064 --> 00:18:28,023
[SNIFFLES]

263
00:18:28,107 --> 00:18:30,359
I never meant for this to happen.

264
00:18:31,652 --> 00:18:35,614
But when I saw their house burning down,

265
00:18:36,615 --> 00:18:39,451
I thought that they deserved it.

266
00:18:39,535 --> 00:18:42,162
So they could go through
what happened to us.

267
00:18:42,246 --> 00:18:44,039
What happened to your sister.

268
00:18:44,123 --> 00:18:49,837
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

269
00:18:49,920 --> 00:18:51,588
But it's also my fault, Ma.

270
00:18:54,049 --> 00:18:55,884
I was followed. [CLICKS TONGUE]

271
00:18:57,511 --> 00:18:59,429
They tracked us down,

272
00:18:59,513 --> 00:19:01,098
and now look where we are.

273
00:19:03,767 --> 00:19:05,185
Behind bars.

274
00:19:05,269 --> 00:19:11,817
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

275
00:19:11,900 --> 00:19:13,443
I will do everything possible, Ma.

276
00:19:16,196 --> 00:19:18,699
I will do everything I can
to get you out of here.

277
00:19:21,994 --> 00:19:23,203
Not just me.

278
00:19:24,580 --> 00:19:25,831
Both of us.

279
00:19:25,914 --> 00:19:29,960
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

280
00:19:30,043 --> 00:19:31,295
Both of us.

281
00:19:34,381 --> 00:19:35,841
[SNIFFLES]

282
00:19:45,934 --> 00:19:46,852
[SNIFFLES]

283
00:19:46,935 --> 00:19:52,524
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

284
00:20:07,789 --> 00:20:13,086
[MAN] <i>I'm afraid I have some bad news.</i>
<i>Your eldest daughter, Abigail?</i>

285
00:20:13,170 --> 00:20:14,796
<i>She died in a fire.</i>

286
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:16,131
<i>Abi, dear…</i>

287
00:20:16,715 --> 00:20:17,925
<i>I promise</i>

288
00:20:18,008 --> 00:20:20,636
<i>I will find your mother and sister.</i>

289
00:20:20,719 --> 00:20:23,138
<i>Billy, are you sure you're ready?</i>

290
00:20:24,348 --> 00:20:26,475
<i>We don't really have a choice.</i>

291
00:20:26,558 --> 00:20:28,852
<i>LoveList can't afford to slow down now.</i>

292
00:20:28,936 --> 00:20:30,103
<i>So to start,</i>

293
00:20:30,187 --> 00:20:33,273
<i>Claire Fabrizio</i>
<i>has officially expressed her interest</i>

294
00:20:33,357 --> 00:20:35,692
<i>in investing in LoveList's</i>
<i>global expansion.</i>

295
00:20:35,776 --> 00:20:37,527
<i>Peter's wife?</i>

296
00:20:37,611 --> 00:20:39,363
<i>We really don't have a choice.</i>

297
00:20:39,446 --> 00:20:42,324
<i>We need to close this deal</i>
<i>with Claire Fabrizio.</i>

298
00:20:42,407 --> 00:20:43,450
<i>Okay?</i>

299
00:20:43,533 --> 00:20:45,327
<i>Multiple charges were filed against you.</i>

300
00:20:45,911 --> 00:20:48,580
<i>You need to apologize to the victim.</i>

301
00:20:49,289 --> 00:20:51,333
<i>I should apologize?!</i>

302
00:20:51,416 --> 00:20:54,253
<i>I will never apologize to that woman!</i>

303
00:20:54,336 --> 00:20:56,838
<i>I don't know if Billy will ever</i>
<i>be able to forgive me</i>

304
00:20:56,922 --> 00:20:58,507
<i>for what I'm about to tell her.</i>

305
00:20:58,590 --> 00:21:00,968
<i>I know this is too much.</i>

306
00:21:01,051 --> 00:21:03,095
<i>But she needs to</i>
<i>know the truth.</i>

307
00:21:03,178 --> 00:21:07,891
<i>You need to tell me why</i>
<i>you're so angry at Ms. Cariño.</i>
